<li><strong>Support pre-readers:</strong> the natural voice helps, but headphones and your presence are still necessary during the first few days.</li>
<li><strong>Be inclusive:</strong> form mixed-ability pairs, respect different paces and use individual assignments for students who need a different level.</li>
<li><strong>Use gamification in moderation:</strong> stars should motivate children, not rank them.</li>
