<li><strong>Hackers (ages 10 to 12 and up):</strong> they write JavaScript or Python in a real editor, with autocomplete and error warnings. They get as far as arrays, objects, <em>for</em> loops, events, error handling and search, sorting and pathfinding algorithms.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Every challenge, read out loud</h3>
<p>Instructions are narrated by a human voice in Spanish. The megaphone button repeats them as many times as needed, with no penalty.</p>
<h3>Large tiles and pieces introduced gradually</h3>
<p>The arrows are chunky, designed for small fingers, and the first ten worlds don’t contain a single written word. Children start with four arrows; loops, conditionals and functions arrive once the child has mastered what came before.</p>
